023-12-18T07:02:32Z","updated_at":"2023-12-18T07:02:32Z","body":"Note that Richard did some investigation: https://gitlab.com/fedora/legal/fedora-license-data/-/issues/425#note_1698073865","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1859661669/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1863344661","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1863344661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1863344661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vEGIV","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-19T19:19:29Z","updated_at":"2023-12-19T19:19:29Z","body":"so... this is essentially the same as [`OpenSSL`](https://spdx.org/licenses/OpenSSL.html) which is a compound license (two licenses in one id - I'm pretty sure we labored over this decision way back when...) but with the order of the two parts reversed. \r\n\r\nI'd agree with @richardfontana  assessment in the Fedora Gitlab issue that \"It's hard to see why the conjunction of the SSLeay license and the (first half of the) OpenSSL license, in that order, shouldn't be treated as equivalent to OpenSSL. But we should get SPDX to weigh in.\"\r\nThere is no substantive difference.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure how we make the order reversible as that is not something our markup can accommodate.  We could of course add something in the Note, but that's not particularly helpful for scanning tools\r\n@goneall @zvr @swinslow  - any thoughts on this? \r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1863344661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1863535994","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1863535994","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1863535994,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vE016","user":{"login":"goneall","id":378172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3ODE3Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/378172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall","html_url":"https://github.com/goneall","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-19T22:04:33Z","updated_at":"2023-12-19T22:04:33Z","body":"I can't think of an easy way to make the order reversible without a very complicated and somewhat impractical regex.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1863535994/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1865528713","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1865528713","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1865528713,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vMbWJ","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-21T05:56:13Z","updated_at":"2023-12-21T05:56:13Z","body":"> I can't think of an easy way to make the order reversible without a very complicated and somewhat impractical regex.\r\n\r\nthanks @goneall - that's what I figured. While not typical, do you think adding a Note as to allowing the reverse order would be helpful? Not tool readable, but it seems crazy to add another license for the same combo but in a different order.\r\n\r\nUnless we broke them apart... sigh","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1865528713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866516578","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1866516578","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1866516578,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vQMhi","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-21T15:40:59Z","updated_at":"2023-12-21T15:40:59Z","body":"I don't understand why you need a regex. Based on what I've seen and some common sense, I doubt most scanners even correctly implement the alt or optional tags in some of the license XML files, if they even attempt to do so. IMO the approach should not be trying to accommodate the primitive state of scanning tools, but to encourage the development of more sophisticated approaches to scanning. If there's a \"note\" in an XML file indicating that an alternative configuration of license texts is a match, a scanning tool should attempt to implement that. \r\n\r\nAnd SPDX gave some consideration to creating an umbrella identifier for \"public domain\". Wouldn't this require an XML file with a large set of alternative license texts? \r\n\r\nI guess Fedora could deal with this by not using `OpenSSL` and instead defining a new `LicenseRef-OpenSSL` which would encompass both SPDX `OpenSSL` as well as this variation. \r\n ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866516578/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866742866","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1866742866","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1866742866,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vRDxS","user":{"login":"goneall","id":378172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3ODE3Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/378172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall","html_url":"https://github.com/goneall","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-21T18:21:17Z","updated_at":"2023-12-21T18:21:17Z","body":"> I don't understand why you need a regex.\r\n\r\nThe use of the license templates have been around for quite a few years and have used regexes to implement the license matching guidelines.  It is implemented in the SPDX Java tools command line and in the SPDX online tools.  There are also some users of the Java library that implement the matching guidelines in other tools (hence some of the template fixes recently submitted).  \r\n\r\nAlthough agree there are quite a few scanners out there that do not implement or honor the license matching guidelines, IMO that doesn't mean we should only support the least common denominator of tool functionality.\r\n\r\nThe implication of not implementing this in the template is that this particular variant will not get matched using the license matching guidelines.  I don't know how popular this variant is - it may not be popular enough to create a practical issue.  In that case a note would be fine.\r\n\r\nOne other consideration is if this technically meets the [License Matching Guidelines](https://spdx.github.io/spdx-spec/v2.3/license-matching-guidelines-and-templates/) as there is no mention that the order of the paragraphs.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866742866/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866835172","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1866835172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1866835172,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vRaTk","user":{"login":"zvr","id":136705,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjcwNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/136705?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr","html_url":"https://github.com/zvr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-21T19:40:05Z","updated_at":"2023-12-21T19:40:05Z","body":"After thinking about this, maybe the easiest (and most future-proof) solution would be to consider that a license does not have a _single_ text but may have more than one associated with a short identifier.\r\nYes, it's a major change, but once decided it can be implemented pretty painlessly: change the XML schema, the model, add a loop while processing in the libs, etc.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866835172/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866860593","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1866860593","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1866860593,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vRggx","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-21T20:02:48Z","updated_at":"2023-12-21T20:02:48Z","body":"@goneall Given that OpenSSL underwent a major license change to `Apache-2.0` in recent years, and also given what I think is a decline in certain practices involving copying of individual source files from project to project, it seems unlikely that this variant will be frequently encountered in the future even with the use of relatively sophisticated scanning tools. \r\n\r\nI think it used to be somewhat common (if disturbing) to see entire OpenSSL releases bundled in open source and proprietary codebases, but in those cases you'd encounter the 'standard' `OpenSSL` license  in the LICENSE file or whatever. Here what happened was a project used *one* source file from OpenSSL and copied over the license notices in that source file rather than the form in which the license appears in the LICENSE file. I'm guessing that is not a common scenario with respect to OpenSSL.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866860593/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866869984","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1866869984","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1866869984,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vRizg","user":{"login":"goneall","id":378172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3ODE3Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/378172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall","html_url":"https://github.com/goneall","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goneall/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-21T20:06:48Z","updated_at":"2023-12-21T20:06:48Z","body":"> After thinking about this, maybe the easiest (and most future-proof) solution would be to consider that a license does not have a single text but may have more than one associated with a short identifier.\r\n\r\nNot a bad solution.  It would slow down the matching a bit, but it would solve this problem.  Due to the performance, I would strongly prefer using the `alt` and `optional` tags, but I'm OK updating the tools if we decide to go in this direction.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866869984/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866950787","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1866950787","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1866950787,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vR2iD","user":{"login":"zvr","id":136705,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjcwNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/136705?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr","html_url":"https://github.com/zvr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zvr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-12-21T21:26:44Z","updated_at":"2023-12-21T21:27:00Z","body":"I didn't explain myself well, @goneall .  I propose we have the exact same setup we currently have (with `alt` and `optional`, etc.), but we also allow, in extreme cases like this one, the possibility to have more than one template associated with a license.\r\nFor almost all cases there would not be a performance hit; only when nothing else works we will introduce a second template to be able to match texts significantly different than the first.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1866950787/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1874432571","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1874432571","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1874432571,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vuZI7","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-01-02T19:08:47Z","updated_at":"2024-01-02T19:10:42Z","body":"ok, so there's a lot here and thanks for the comments!  \r\nit sounds like, for the time being, we should add a note, which I've proposed here: https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/pull/2295\r\n\r\nAs for @zvr - I'm not entirely sure how that would work, or if we'd need that for more than this license (would that be a change proposal?)? But maybe we should move that idea to its own issue and discuss.\r\n\r\nAlso not sure if what @zvr is proposing and the public domain proposal I floated on the email list some time ago that @richardfontana referenced are the same?\r\n\r\n@goneall - we do sort of address ordering... of paragraphs in B3.2. https://spdx.github.io/spdx-spec/v2.3/license-matching-guidelines-and-templates/ but not exactly addressed to compound licenses scenario... ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1874432571/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1874433558","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1874433558","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1874433558,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vuZYW","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-01-02T19:09:46Z","updated_at":"2024-01-02T19:09:46Z","body":"meant to add: just trying to move things along, as Fedora package maintainers are held-up on a number of SPDX issues, so going for the \"path of least resistance\" solution now. but can reconsider better options later?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1874433558/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1874494824","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1874494824","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1874494824,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vuoVo","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-01-02T20:10:22Z","updated_at":"2024-01-02T20:10:22Z","body":"Worth noting here that this is what is encountered in a libgit2 source file: https://github.com/libgit2/libgit2/blob/main/COPYING#L1030C1-L1133\r\n\r\nIt is not exactly \"the OpenSSL license with the two pieces in reverse order\", but it is almost that. It is the SSLeay license (conceptually the second license in the OpenSSL license) followed seemingly coincidentally by the first half (the OpenSSL license proper), along with a bunch of other license notices preceding it and following it. Interestingly, the libgit2 source file refers to this as \"the OpenSSL license\". But it doesn't have the glue paragraph that is situated between the OpenSSL license proper and the SSLeay license in the \"canonical\" OpenSSL license. I don't know how much that matters. \r\n\r\nThat missing paragraph, which is currently mandatory in SPDX `OpenSSL`, is:\r\n```\r\n This product includes cryptographic software written by Eric Young\r\n (eay@cryptsoft.com).  This product includes software written by Tim\r\n Hudson (tjh@cryptsoft.com).\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1874494824/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1874496181","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1874496181","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1874496181,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vuoq1","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-01-02T20:11:50Z","updated_at":"2024-01-02T20:12:17Z","body":"> ok, so there's a lot here and thanks for the comments! it sounds like, for the time being, we should add a note, which I've proposed here: #2295\r\n \r\n@jlovejoy This note is not sufficient because it doesn't account for the [missing paragraph](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1874494824).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1874496181/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1874774912","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1874774912","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1874774912,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85vvsuA","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-01-03T02:21:15Z","updated_at":"2024-01-03T02:21:15Z","body":"good catch @richardfontana - not sure if this further breaks stuff, but I'm suggesting that can be optional as it's more informative and have added an optional tag to my PR\r\n\r\nOf course, need other eyes on this... it's not an optimal solution, but maybe a good tie-over? ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1874774912/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1887652738","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275#issuecomment-1887652738","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2275","id":1887652738,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85wg0uC","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-01-11T17:37:11Z","updated_at":"2024-01-11T17:37:11Z","body":"Discussed on 2024-01-11 legal team call:\r\n\r\n* decided to keep OpenSSL as-is on the license list currently\r\n* however, will add two new entries, `OpenSSL-standalone` with top half on its own, and `SSLeay-standalone` with bottom half on its own\r\n* will also make \"This product includes...\" notice language optional","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1887652738/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]